f now, India has signed extradition treaties\nwith a total of 50 countries and entered into extradition arrangements with 10\nmore countries to facilitate extradition. Out of these, 4 extradition treaties\nwere signed in the last 3 years. In the last three years, 11 fugitive criminals\nfrom various foreign countries, including the recent extradition of Christian\nMichel from UAE, were successfully brought back to India.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|16|UNSTARRED |395", "t": "Annual Plan Outlay for Bihar", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PLANNING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED  QUESTION NO. 395 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 12.12.2018 \n \nANNUAL PLAN OUTLAY FOR BIHAR \n \n395.   DR. SANJAY JAISWAL: \n \n \nWill the Minister of PLANNING be pleased to state: \n(a) the details of annual plan outlay for Bihar for the last three years;  \n(b) the details of proposals under which the money was spent, project-wise; and  \n(c)  the mechanism of monitoring of the same by the Union Government?  \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF \nPLANNING AND MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND \nFERTILIZERS \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) to (c.) : The annual plan outlay for the State was finalized by the Planning \nCommission and the State Government up to 2014 -15. The mandate of the NITI Aayog does \nnot include finalization of the Annual Plan Outlay from 1st January 2015. \nHowever the desired information as available on Bihar Government website is attached as \nAnnex. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnex to LS US no 395 to be answered on 12.12,18 \n \nBUDGET ESTIMATE (BE) 2018-2019 RELATED TO SERVICES AT A GLANCE                                           (  Rs.in Crores) \nSubject 2016-2017 (Actual) 2017-2018 (BE) 2017-2018 (RE) 2018-2019 (BE) \nAmount Percent Amount Percent Amount Percent Amount Percent \n1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 \nA. Head of Receipts         \n1. State's Share in Central Taxes 58880.59 46.30 65326.34 40.57 65083.1