rehabilitation of \nforest villages. The details of funds provided for such relocation and rehabilitation is \ngiven in the Annexure-II (a) and II(b). \n \n (d) &(e) Rehabilitation of villages is a voluntary process. Hence no deadline has been fixed.  \n \n***  \n\n \nAnnexure-I \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF THE LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 816 DUE FOR ANSWER ON 14.12.2018 ASKED BY SHRI AJAY NISHAD \nREGARDING VILLAGES IN FOREST AREAS \n \nStatement showing total No. of forest villages in various States \n \nS.N. State  Total No. of Villages \n1 Assam  499 \n2 Chhattisgarh  425 \n3 Gujarat  199 \n4 Himachal Pradesh     0 \n5 Jharkhand    24 \n6 Madhya Pradesh  893 \n7 Meghalaya    23 \n8 Mizoram    85 \n9 Odisha    20 \n10 Tripura    62 \n11 Uttarakhand    61 \n12 Uttar Pradesh    13 \n13 West Bengal  170 \nA Sub total 2,474 \n \nInformation available for number of villages only for core/critical Tiger Reserve area in the \nfollowing States  \n \nS.No. State No. of villages inside the \ncore/critical tiger habitat \n13 Andhra Pradesh  28 \n14 Arunachal Pradesh   3 \n15 Bihar   0 \n15 Karnataka 102 \n16 Kerala    0 \n17 Maharashtra  33 \n18 Rajasthan  82 \n19 Tamil Nadu  49 \n20 Telangana  37 \n21 Uttrakhand   0 \nB Sub total 3,34 \n Grand Total (A+B)= \n \n2,808 \n \n \n  \n\nAnnexure-II(a) \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b) & (c) OF THE LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 816 DUE FOR ANSWER ON 14.12.2018 ASKED BY SHRI \nAJAY NISHAD REGARDING VILLAGES IN FOREST AREAS \n \nState-wise details of funds released during last three years for the voluntary relocation of families \nfrom the Protected Areas under the Centrally Sponsored Scheme of “Development of Wildlife \nHabitats” during the last three years \n \n(Rs. in lakh) \n \nS.No. Name of State Village/sancuary Year \n2015-16 \n \n2016-17 2017-18 \n1. Kerala Kurchiyat 270.00  - - \nChettiyalathur - 1108.80 - \n2. Mizoram Kawanpuri West, \nDarangawn West and \nThorangthlang \nWild