Centre for Natural Product Research (NCNPR) University of\nMississippi, USA.\n\n-2-\nMinistry participated in 9th EU -India Joint Working Group on Pharmaceuticals,\nBiotechnology and Medical Devices held on 27th -28th September, 2018 at Brussels for\nrecognition/ promotion of AYUSH Medicine abroad especially in Europe. Ministry also got\nparticipated as observer in Committee on Herbal Medicinal Products (HMPC) meeting.\nMinistry has established dialogue with National Agency for Drug and Food Control,\nIndonesia for cooperation and collaboration in the field of traditional systems of medicine.\n(c) & (d): Pharmacopoeia Commission for Indian Medicine & Homoeopathy (PCIM&H) an\nautonomous body under Ministry of AYUSH for developing standards for Ayurveda, Sidhha,\nUnani & Homeopathy (ASU&H) system of medicines, has signed MoU on 10th April, 2015 with\nIndian Council of Medical Research (ICMR) to secure the isolated phyto -compounds and\nassociated scientific data in such manner that facilitates their appropriate usage towards\ndevelopment of pharmacopoeial standards and other research of national importance.\n\nAnnexure\nState wise/System wise Number of AYUSH Hospitals as on 1-4-2017\nS.\nNo\n.\nState / UT Ayurve\nda\nUnan\ni\nSiddh\na\nYog\na Naturopat\nhy\nHomoeop\nathy\nSowa-\nRigpa Total\nA. States/Union\nTerritories\n1 Andhra Pradesh 3 2 0 0 0 3 0 8\n2\nArunachal\nPradesh 10 0 0 0 0 2 0 12\n3 Assam 1 0 0 0 0 3 0 4\n4 Bihar 5 1 0 0 0 2 0 8\n5 Chhattisgarh 10 1 0 1 0 3 0 15\n6 Delhi 2 1 0 0 0 2 0 5\n7 Goa 1 0 0 0 0 1 0 2\n8 Gujarat 42 0 0 0 6 16 0 64\n9 Haryana 9 1 0 0 0 1 0 11\n10 Himachal Pradesh 33 0 0 0 1 0 0 34\n11\nJammu &\nKashmir 1 1 0 0 0 0 0 2\n12 Jharkhand 1 0 0 0 0 4 0 5\n13 Karnataka 170 18 0 3 6 16 0 213\n14 Kerala 126 0 1 0 1 34 0 162\n15 Madhya Pradesh 21 0 0 0 0 2 0 23\n16 Maharashtra 64 6 0 0 0 1 0 71\n17 Manipur 2 1 0 1 0 6 0 10\n18 Meghalaya 3 0 0 0 0 7 0 10\n19 Mizoram 1 0 0 0 0 1 0 2\n20 Nagaland 1 0 0 0 0 1 0 2\n21 Odisha 8 0 0 0 0 6 0 14\n22 